    "notes": "Reached 100% PASS after fixing three implementation bugs, each found via actually running the scripts rather than by code review alone: (1) an MPS/CPU torch.Generator device mismatch inside the sampling helper (_sample), surfaced by scripts/p1_rejection_sampling.py; (2) the greedy-mode rejection branch incorrectly reused the residual-resampling formula that is only correct for sampling mode, instead of returning the target model's own argmax -- violates the greedy-equivalence proof; (3) a round can emit up to gamma+1 tokens (the +1 being the bonus token), which was not being truncated at EOS or at the max_new_tokens budget, causing spec-decode output to be exactly 1 token longer than the reference in 3 of 5 prompts on the first PASS attempt (0 mismatched positions even then -- only a length/budget bug, not a token-value bug)."
